{"id":"m68851:glossary-def:fs-idm27477328-def","rulings":["atom","nucleon"],"maxOps":6,"en":"energy lost when an atom’s nucleons are bound together (or the energy needed to break a nucleus into its constituent protons and neutrons)","is":"orka sem tapast þegar kjarneindir atóms bindast saman (eða orkan sem þarf til að brjóta kjarna í sundur í róteindir og nifteindir)"},
{"id":"m68851:glossary-term:fs-idm41591488-term","rulings":["nucleon"],"maxOps":6,"en":"nucleon","is":"kjarneind"},
{"id":"m68851:glossary-def:fs-idp188698800-def","rulings":["nucleon"],"maxOps":9,"en":"phenomenon exhibited by an unstable nucleon that spontaneously undergoes change into a nucleon that is more stable; an unstable nucleon is said to be radioactive","is":"fyrirbæri sem óstöðug kjarneind sýnir þegar hún breytist sjálfkrafa í stöðugri kjarneind; óstöðug kjarneind er sögð vera geislavirk"},
{"id":"m68851:glossary-def:fs-idp26284960-def","rulings":["nucleon"],"maxOps":6,"en":"force of attraction between nucleons that holds a nucleus together","is":"aðdráttarkraftur milli kjarneinda sem heldur kjarna saman"}
]}

